{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":58074996,"ns":0,"title":"Canberra Plan","extract":"In philosophy, the Canberra Plan is a contemporary program of methodology and analysis which answers questions about what the world is like according to physics. It is considered a naturalistic approach in metaphysics, which holds that metaphysics can explain the features of the world described by physics and what the different classes of everyday belief represent.","description":"Philosophical method","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}